IMPORT prelude

-- District Cooling Act 2001 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for an occupier, a landowner, a developer, a contractor who digs, and
-- a business that sells chilled water: the duty to use district cooling in a service area and the licensee's duty to supply (s 7),
-- the licence requirement and the Authority's financial penalty (ss 10, 11, 13, 32), entry onto premises by the Authority (s 6) and
-- by the licensee (ss 25, 27), the landowner's right to have the system moved (s 28), the licensee's apparatus (s 30), emergency
-- discontinuance (ss 17, 31), the appeal windows (ss 10(8), 12(4), 13(2), 25(10), 28(8)), and the offences, penalties, composition
-- and officers' liability (ss 5, 32 to 35, 37 to 41).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation --
-- version in force from 1/4/2022, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/DCA2001.txt. The latest amendment annotated in the
-- body is Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022 (s 30); Act 37 of 2021 wef 29/01/2022 (ss 21, 46, 47) and S 26/2022 wef 13/01/2022
-- (s 22(5)) are also shown. The deposit's metadata says "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0091 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the provisions an occupier, landowner, developer, excavating contractor or would-be supplier meets. Not
-- encoded: the Authority's administration (ss 3, 4), declaring and revoking service areas (ss 7(1), (2), 8, 9), licence conditions
-- and their modification beyond the appeal window (ss 10(2) to (7), 12), codes of practice and directions (ss 14 to 16), the
-- licensee's general duties and pricing (ss 18, 19 -- s 19(2) forbids undue preference or discrimination, which is not reducible
-- to a test here), the register (s 20), special administration (ss 21 to 23), entry onto public land (s 24), wayleaves (s 26), the
-- developer's duty to provide space (s 29), court jurisdiction (s 36), Minister's appeals generally (s 42), exemptions (s 43), service
-- of documents (s 44), and regulations, incorporation by reference and advisory guidelines (ss 45 to 47). No regulations were
-- retrieved, so which offences are compoundable (s 40(2)) is unknown.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `District Cooling Act 2001 -- consumers, land and offences`

§§ `7 -- the duty to use district cooling, and the duty to supply`

-- s 7(3): "Unless exempted, the occupier of every premises within a service area requiring air conditioning must use the district
-- cooling services provided by a licensee if the services are available within the service area."
-- s 7(4): an owner or occupier "may apply in writing to the Authority for exemption from subsection (3) and the decision of the
-- Authority is final". (s 43 also lets the Authority, with the Minister's approval, exempt any person or premises.)
-- s 7(5): "A licensee must not refuse to provide district cooling services to any premises within the licensee's service area."
-- s 7(6): contravening (3) or (5) -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both, and for a
-- continuing offence "a further fine not exceeding $250 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- conviction".
GIVEN `in a service area` IS A BOOLEAN, `requires air conditioning` IS A BOOLEAN, `services are available` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupier must use district cooling` IF
    `in a service area` AND `requires air conditioning` AND `services are available` AND (NOT `exempted`)

GIVEN `in a service area` IS A BOOLEAN, `requires air conditioning` IS A BOOLEAN, `services are available` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted` IS A BOOLEAN, `uses district cooling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupier commits a s 7 offence` IF
    `the occupier must use district cooling` `in a service area` `requires air conditioning` `services are available` `exempted`
    AND (NOT `uses district cooling`)

-- The duty to supply has no exception in s 7 itself; s 31 (below) lets the licensee DISCONTINUE supply in an emergency.
GIVEN `premises are in the licensee's service area` IS A BOOLEAN, `the licensee refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee commits a s 7 offence` IF
    `premises are in the licensee's service area` AND `the licensee refused`

-- The daily further fine is counted per day or part of a day after conviction; the count is taken as given.
GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for a continuing s 7 offence` MEANS
    10000 PLUS 250 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `10, 11, 32 -- the licence`

-- s 10(1): "A person must not provide district cooling services to any service area unless the person is authorised to do so by a
-- licence." s 11: "A licence is not transferable and any purported transfer of any licence is void."
-- s 32: providing district cooling services without a licence -- "a fine not exceeding $50,000" (no imprisonment).
-- s 2: "district cooling service" means "the sale of coolant for space cooling in a service area by a licensee operating a central
-- plant capable of supplying coolant via pipe to more than one building in the service area".
GIVEN `was granted a licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `received a licence by transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person holds a licence` IF
    `was granted a licence`

GIVEN `provides district cooling services to a service area` IS A BOOLEAN, `was granted a licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `received a licence by transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provider commits the s 32 offence` IF
    `provides district cooling services to a service area`
    AND (NOT (`the person holds a licence` `was granted a licence` `received a licence by transfer`))

§§ `13(1)(i) -- the Authority's financial penalty`

-- s 13(1)(i): "a financial penalty not exceeding 10% of the annual turnover derived from the provisions of district cooling services
-- by the licensee in Singapore as ascertained from its latest audited accounts". Grounds (s 13(1)(a) to (d)) include a contravention
-- of the licence, a code of practice, the Act or a direction, liquidation, a composition with creditors, or "the public interest or
-- security of Singapore". It is imposed "without any liability for compensation".
GIVEN `annual district cooling turnover in Singapore` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum financial penalty` MEANS
    `annual district cooling turnover in Singapore` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `10(8), 12(4), 13(2), 25(10), 28(8) -- appeals to the Minister`

-- Each appeal lies to the Minister "whose decision is final", within 14 days: s 10(8) "within 14 days of the refusal" to grant or
-- renew a licence; s 12(4) "within 14 days of the receipt by the licensee of the direction"; s 13(2) "within 14 days after the date of
-- the notice"; s 25(10) "within 14 days of the conclusion of the inquiry"; s 28(8) "within 14 days of the decision".
-- Day counting is not modelled: the cases take the number of days since the trigger event as given, and day 14 is treated as within
-- time (an inference from "within").
GIVEN `days since the triggering event` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `days since the triggering event` AT MOST 14

§§ `6 -- entry by the Authority`

-- s 6(1): the Authority may by its employees, agents or contractors "enter at all reasonable hours (or at any time in the event of an
-- emergency)" into any premises, without liability to pay any fee, charge or expense.
-- s 6(2): "Except in the event of an emergency", they may not enter unless "(a) not less than 6 hours' notice of the intended entry
-- has been given to the occupier; and (b) if required to do so, he or she has produced evidence of his or her authority."
GIVEN `an emergency` IS A BOOLEAN, `at a reasonable hour` IS A BOOLEAN, `hours of notice given` IS A NUMBER, `the occupier asked for evidence of authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `evidence of authority produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may enter` IF
        `an emergency`
    OR  (    `at a reasonable hour`
         AND `hours of notice given` AT LEAST 6
         AND ((NOT `the occupier asked for evidence of authority`) OR `evidence of authority produced`))

§§ `25 -- the licensee laying the system on private land`

-- s 25(1): the licensee may enter land in the service area, other than public land, to survey and to lay or erect the system,
-- "paying compensation to any person interested for any damage or financial loss". (3): the licensee acquires no right "other than
-- that of a user only".
-- s 25(5): "a licensee must give at least 14 days' notice". (6): the owner or occupier "may, within 14 days of the receipt of the
-- notice ... lodge a written objection with the Authority". (7): "If no objection is lodged within the time specified in
-- subsection (5), the licensee may forthwith enter". (8), (9): if an objection is lodged and not withdrawn, the Authority must hold an
-- inquiry and may then authorise the acts.
-- The time for objecting is in (6), not (5): s 25(7) cross-refers to the wrong subsection. Read here as the 14 days in (6). The text
-- does not say what happens when an objection is lodged and then withdrawn; that case is not modelled.
GIVEN `days since receipt of the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the objection is in time` IF
    `days since receipt of the notice` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `days of notice given` IS A NUMBER, `an objection was lodged in time` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Authority authorised after inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee may enter to lay the system` IF
    `days of notice given` AT LEAST 14
    AND ((NOT `an objection was lodged in time`) OR `the Authority authorised after inquiry`)

§§ `27 -- the licensee inspecting and repairing`

-- s 27(1): to inspect, maintain or repair the system the licensee may, "after giving 7 days' prior notice to the owner or occupier of
-- any land", at any reasonable time enter land or a building in the service area, "causing as little damage as possible and paying
-- compensation". (2): "in the event of an operational emergency arising from any fault in a district cooling system, pipe or plant, no
-- prior notice is required". There is no objection procedure, unlike s 25.
GIVEN `days of notice given` IS A NUMBER, `an operational emergency from a fault` IS A BOOLEAN, `at a reasonable hour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee may enter to inspect or repair` IF
    `at a reasonable hour` AND (`an operational emergency from a fault` OR `days of notice given` AT LEAST 7)

§§ `28 -- the landowner's right to have the system moved`

-- s 28(10): "owner" includes "any person having a leasehold interest with an unexpired term of not less than 7 years".
-- s 28(1): an owner who wants to use the land so that the system should be moved or altered "may require the licensee to remove or
-- alter" it; (2), (3) the Authority inquires if the licensee fails to comply. Who pays is NOT stated.
-- s 28(4), (5): for development, the owner may request removal, and if the licensee does the work "the owner is liable to pay
-- reasonable compensation to the licensee".
-- s 28(7): a part "no longer in use" -- the licensee must on request remove it "at its own cost and expense and compensate the owner".
-- s 28(9): the section "does not apply where a contrary intention has been expressed by the owner of the land and the licensee by
-- agreement".
GIVEN `holds the freehold` IS A BOOLEAN, `unexpired years of lease` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an owner for s 28` IF
    `holds the freehold` OR `unexpired years of lease` AT LEAST 7

DECLARE `Removal Reason` IS ONE OF
    `the owner wants to use the land differently`
    `the owner wants to develop the land`
    `the part is no longer in use`

DECLARE Payer IS ONE OF
    `the owner pays the licensee`
    `the licensee bears the cost`
    `the Act does not say`

GIVEN `the reason` IS A `Removal Reason`
GIVETH A Payer
`who pays for removal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `the owner wants to develop the land` THEN `the owner pays the licensee`
    WHEN `the part is no longer in use` THEN `the licensee bears the cost`
    OTHERWISE `the Act does not say`

GIVEN `holds the freehold` IS A BOOLEAN, `unexpired years of lease` IS A NUMBER, `agreed otherwise with the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may require removal` IF
    `is an owner for s 28` `holds the freehold` `unexpired years of lease` AND (NOT `agreed otherwise with the licensee`)

§§ `30 -- the licensee's apparatus on the consumer's premises`

-- s 30: apparatus "owned or let for hire or lent to a consumer by a licensee" and affixed to the consumer's premises "(a) continues
-- to remain the property of that licensee and is deemed not to be a fixture, and does not vest in the owner of the premises; and
-- (b) shall not be subject to distress or be liable to be taken under ... an enforcement order of any court or any proceedings in
-- bankruptcy or winding up proceedings against the party in whose possession it is".
GIVEN `supplied by the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the apparatus vests in the owner of the premises` IF
    NOT `supplied by the licensee`

GIVEN `supplied by the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the apparatus can be taken in the consumer's bankruptcy or winding up` IF
    NOT `supplied by the licensee`

§§ `17, 31 -- emergency discontinuance and liability`

-- s 31(1): where the licensee "is of the opinion that immediate action is necessary on the occurrence of any emergency, in the
-- interests of public safety or in order to avoid undue interference with the efficient provision of district cooling services to
-- other consumers or for any other reasons affecting the public interest", it "may forthwith discontinue" supply to any consumer.
-- (2): it must then give written notice to the Authority and the consumer and restore supply "as soon as is reasonably
-- practicable". (3): "A licensee shall not be liable for any loss or damage caused to any person resulting from such
-- discontinuance." s 17: the Authority "shall not be liable in any circumstances" for loss from a licensee's default.
-- The notice duty in (2) is not a condition of the immunity in (3) on the words; the immunity attaches to "such discontinuance".
GIVEN `the licensee formed the s 31 opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee may discontinue supply` IF
    `the licensee formed the s 31 opinion`

GIVEN `the licensee formed the s 31 opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee is immune from liability for the cut-off` IF
    `the licensee may discontinue supply` `the licensee formed the s 31 opinion`

§§ `38 -- digging in a service area`

-- s 38: "Any person who digs, bores, trenches, grades, excavates or breaks any ground with any mechanical equipment or explosive within
-- the service area or allows that person's employee or agent to do so without first ascertaining the location of any apparatus
-- belonging to or under the management or control of a licensee that may be interfered with shall be guilty of an offence."
-- Digging by hand is outside the words.
GIVEN `within a service area` IS A BOOLEAN, `with mechanical equipment or explosive` IS A BOOLEAN, `first ascertained where the apparatus is` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the excavation is an offence` IF
    `within a service area` AND `with mechanical equipment or explosive` AND (NOT `first ascertained where the apparatus is`)

§§ `5, 7, 32 to 35, 37 to 39, 45 -- penalties`

-- s 39: an offence "for which no penalty is expressly provided" -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding
-- 12 months or both. Express penalties: s 7(6) $10,000 or 12 months (plus $250 a day, above); s 32 $50,000 fine only; s 37(3)
-- $5,000 fine only. s 45(2): regulations may make a contravention an offence punishable by up to $5,000 or 6 months or both.
-- No express penalty, so s 39: s 5(2), (3) (notices to furnish information), s 33 (falsely pretending to be an employee of the
-- Authority or a licensee to gain entry), s 34 (obstructing the Authority), s 35 (false statements; procuring a licence by fraud),
-- s 38 (digging without locating the apparatus).
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `failing to comply with a notice to furnish information`
    `failing to use district cooling or refusing to supply`
    `providing district cooling without a licence`
    `pretending to be an employee to gain entry`
    `obstructing the Authority`
    `making a false statement`
    `refusing to give identity or information`
    `digging without locating the apparatus`
    `contravening a regulation`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `providing district cooling without a licence` THEN 50000
    WHEN `refusing to give identity or information` THEN 5000
    WHEN `contravening a regulation` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `providing district cooling without a licence` THEN 0
    WHEN `refusing to give identity or information` THEN 0
    WHEN `contravening a regulation` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 12

§§ `40 -- composition`

-- s 40(1): the Authority "may, in its discretion, compound any offence under this Act which is prescribed as a compoundable offence
-- by collecting ... a sum not exceeding $3,000". (2): the offences are prescribed by regulations (not retrieved).
GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum demanded` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition is within the Act` IF
    `prescribed as compoundable` AND `sum demanded` AT MOST 3000

§§ `41 -- officers of a company or firm`

-- s 41: where an offence is committed by "a company, firm, society or other body of persons" and is "proved to have been committed
-- with the authority, consent or connivance" of a person who was "a director, manager, secretary or other similar officer or a
-- partner ... or was purporting to act in any such capacity", that person "shall also be guilty of that offence". No neglect limb.
GIVEN `the body committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `with the person's authority, consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `an officer or partner, or purporting to be one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
    `the body committed an offence` AND `with the person's authority, consent or connivance` AND `an officer or partner, or purporting to be one`
